  "lineage": "Rural Puerto Rican mountain (montaña) peasant song tradition rooted in the Spanish décima poetic form (ten-line stanza, 8 syllables per line, ABBAACCDDC rhyme scheme) brought from 17th-century Iberian colonial settlement and preserved in the Puerto Rican mountain interior — performed on the cuatro puertorriqueño (the 10-string national instrument with five double-string courses), classical guitar, güiro, and bongos; figures Ramito (Florencio Morales Ramos, the 20th-century jíbaro voice), Chuíto el de Bayamón, Toño Mayo, and the modern revival through Ecos de Borinquen and the Cuatro Project",
